# The Raspberry Pi 2 with a process address space of its own for every process
# (CONF_WITH_PROCESS_ASPACES, #568): EmuCON and the programs it runs are in
# user mode, each in its own page tables, the kernel half of the address space
# is supervisor-only, and a fault in a process ends that process only.  No
# desktop yet (doc/mmu-address-space.txt, "The screen"); the console is on the
# UART as well, for QEMU's raspi2b machine.
MACHINE_RPI=y
TARGET_RPI2=y
CONF_SERIAL_CONSOLE=y
CONF_WITH_AES=n
CONF_WITH_PROCESS_ASPACES=y
